// Audio adapter for The Walking Trade (procedural). The mixer, reverb rooms, voice pools, footsteps, impacts, reload
// foley, shell clinks, explosions, rain, wind and thunder are Saltline's engine (js/sl/audio-sl.js, generated by
// tools/port-sl-audio.js from Saltline by Felix Rieseberg, claude.ai artifact BGY1SztrAYcJQHSsnHHGmp). The per-class
// gunshot rows below are new recipes written with Saltline's own DSP kit (its `at` noise bursts, `ei` pitch-swept
// thumps, `dn` modal rings, `Se` layering and `Wo` soft clip) in the same layer structure as its rifle (KR): crack,
// snap, thump, body, blat, air, low boom and a mechanical layer; numbers per weapon class are this game's.
// The game's own synthesised one-shots (js/synth.js: bell, coins, register, groans, siren, UI...) play through the
// same context and master chain (attach()), positional ones through a PannerNode into Saltline's world bus.
import { createSaltlineAudio, SOUNDS, KIT } from './sl/audio-sl.js';

